    "summary": "First New Speedway Boogie, wild Lovelight; historic but uneven",
    "blurb": "The set delivers the debut of New Speedway Boogie and a quirky rap rendition of Turn On Your Lovelight. Dark Star flows into Saint Stephen and The Eleven for deep improvisation, though tape hiss and occasional skips temper the listening experience.",
    "review": "On December 20 1969 at San Francisco’s Fillmore Auditorium the Dead rolled out several milestones. Set 1 opened with a solid acoustic‑rock blend before stumbling on a lyrical stumble in High Time, but the real fireworks arrived in the second set: Dark Star segued into Saint Stephen and The Eleven, culminating in the first ever performance of New Speedway Boogie. That tune crackles with fresh energy, and the band’s off‑the‑cuff rap take on Turn On Your Lovelight adds a unique, almost theatrical twist. While the soundboard source captures these moments, it suffers from noticeable tape hiss, occasional CD‑skip on “China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider,” and dropouts around “High Time.” For archivists and completists the historic value outweighs the sonic imperfections, making this recording a worthwhile, if imperfect, snapshot of the Dead’s late‑’69 evolution.",
